This article is for informational purposes only and does not, under any circumstances, constitute investment advice or a recommendation.

The crowdfunding platform ClubFunding has issued the closing report for the fundraising round intended to refinance a commercial asset in Saint-Denis, on the island of Réunion, in order to allow the operator to finance a new real estate acquisition in Saint-Leu. The project is led by the company JOCETHAD, a subsidiary of the Comptemporis group. The subscription process has concluded, consolidating an amount raised of €320,000, above the €175,000 initially announced for the bond issue. Investors should keep in mind that any reference to return is inseparable from the corresponding risk, which is described below.

The campaign completed its raise in a period of 10 days. The analysis of the flow of contributions during that interval records an average contribution ratio of €22 per minute.

Financial Terms of the Operation

The operation is structured through a bond issue and has two guarantees: a first-rank mortgage registered over the asset being financed and a personal and joint guarantee from the director. The issuer recalls that the higher the interest rate, the greater the risk of loss of capital or non-payment of interest, and that past returns are not indicative of future returns. In compliance with the European regulatory framework, non-experienced investors have a four-calendar-day pre-contractual reflection period during which they may revoke their commitment at no cost and without justification.

Asset Description and Operation Plan

The asset is a 112 m² commercial unit located at 20 Rue de Nice, in the Barachois district of Saint-Denis, in a commercial area with high footfall, close to the Radisson hotel and to the city's business and financial center, with car access and several car parks nearby. The property was acquired in 2023 for €300,000 and refurbishment works were carried out to adapt it to the new tenant. The unit has a lease signed in 2024 and running until 31 May 2033, leaving seven years to maturity; in addition, the tenant has invested €200,000 in fitting out and maintaining the premises.

The refinancing allows the operator to release liquidity to acquire a new residential asset in Saint-Leu, while retaining a commercial property that generates recurring rental income. The subsequent objective is to sell the premises with the lease in place for a price of €450,000, that is, approximately €4,018/m².

Operator Profile and Collateral

The operation is promoted by JOCETHAD, a subsidiary of the Comptemporis group, which specializes in real estate operations in Réunion. Among the elements highlighted by the platform are the location of the asset and the lease running until 2033. As a counterpart, the platform notes the existence of illiquidity risk and the risk of total or partial loss of the amounts invested.

Finally, in compliance with the regulations governing crowdfunding platforms, investors are reminded that this is a participatory financing product and not a deposit or a guaranteed savings product, and that real estate investments carry risks of illiquidity and partial or total loss of principal. This project is not supervised by the CNMV or the Bank of Spain, and the invested capital is not covered by the deposit guarantee fund or the investor compensation scheme.

